{"authored" [{"question" "q-152875" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}2\\cdot {5}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "d66ab49cfbf4bb4b39421bffaad0f0d04c5f3f720b25be8a87396f615086604a" "basis" 1336 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-152875" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}2\\cdot {5}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{1}{5}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}]}_{a}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[{5}^{x}]}_{a}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }({5}^{1}-{5}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot (5-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{5}^{a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y={5}^{x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{5}^{x}=0$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{5}^{x}=\\infty $\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/assets/06c51ecc423683f4377248004b7a318f1348836bd752a7f65f94457d1774e64d.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}2\\cdot {5}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot (5-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{5}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot (5-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "d66ab49cfbf4bb4b39421bffaad0f0d04c5f3f720b25be8a87396f615086604a" "basis" 1336 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-152875" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "abaa9270682b58d8b9e9a28aaa831c88fe855525b815e382ccfdc43dfe25035a" "basis" 1336 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-152875" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "d66ab49cfbf4bb4b39421bffaad0f0d04c5f3f720b25be8a87396f615086604a" "basis" 1336 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-152875" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{10}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "d66ab49cfbf4bb4b39421bffaad0f0d04c5f3f720b25be8a87396f615086604a" "basis" 1336 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-152875" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "d66ab49cfbf4bb4b39421bffaad0f0d04c5f3f720b2